":null,"author":"Obe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891164","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891164"}},{"id":"cZcEbLCi5xLONrYWitBho","ext":"jpg","post_id":"6HJ0Gv3abkTqVNiv1L9CS","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Evan Christensen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-04-21T18:27:37.000Z","updated_at":"2024-04-21T18:27:37.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/cZcEbLCi5xLONrYWitBho","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/cZcEbLCi5xLONrYWitBho"}},{"id":"891347","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895244","description":null,"caption":"Views","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Daniel Cottam","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891347","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891347"}},{"id":"891348","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895245","description":null,"caption":"Price @03. Woodside (US 6 Bridge) to confluence with Green River","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891348","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891348"}},{"id":"891349","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895246","description":null,"caption":"Price @03. Woodside (US 6 Bridge) to confluence with Green River","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891349","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891349"}},{"id":"891350","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895247","description":null,"caption":"Biggest Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Daniel  Cottam","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891350","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891350"}},{"id":"891351","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895248","description":null,"caption":"05/19/19","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Daniel Cottam","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891351","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891351"}}],"detail":{"id":"1866","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Scott England mentioned that this run is class II and III. With one brief rapid with a class IV move that is easily portaged at 400 cfs.\n\nThe float is aound 34 miles from the hwy 191 bridge to Swasey's take-out. You can cut off around 12.5 miles of meanders by driving down the canyon on the access road and put it where it crosses the river.  This makes a daily trip easier and avoids almost all of the flat sections of the river.  The road is well maintained and any high clearance vehicle can travel down it.\n\nIt can be run in a long day with 400 CFS.    At 400 cfs the river is almost always chest deep or less with steep cut banks.  Be carefull when getting out and choose your stops wisely.\n\nIn May 2019 Graham Abrams shared: \\[at 500 cfs, about class 3+  but\\]  'there are lots of quick moves and blind corners and not lots of eddies. It’s about a 30 mile section. You can do it in a long day but I did it in 3 days so I could hike/camp.' Minimum good around 250 cfs for packrafts.\n\nThe two major rapids are Long Canyon and Little Big Drop.  You can tell your at LC when you see the giant cobble rocks stacked on the right bank.  It is a great fun read and run.  Little Big Drop should be run on the left and gets easier as the flows get higher.   The rocks in this are easy to recognize and there are nice places to pull off right before the rapid.  Portaging this rapid is easy and short.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"26.7","correlations":[{"reachID":"1866","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"250","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"2000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"PRICE RIVER AT WOODSIDE, UT","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09314500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"6","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"6.63","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"39.26444444","longitude":"-110.3427778"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09314500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09314500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nHigh Runnable (R6-R9): 1001 - 2000 cfs Adjusted Difficulty: IV Comment: IV? Watch for wood moving during seasonal highs. \r\n\r\n\nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 250 - 1000 cfs  Comment: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\nToo Low to Boat (L0-L9): 0 - 200 cfs  Comment: Flow range for best boatability uncertain. Please help your fellow boaters with a comment or report.\n\nMigration Errors: \nDifferent ranges are defining the same values","comment":"Gauge (1540 sq.mi. drainage) is near the put-in for this reach, thus should accurately show actual flow in this reach.","status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"6","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["114922","109669"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-110.342992,39.264415],[-110.342626,39.264406]